00:01:20.900 --> 00:01:28.780
Selling cash-secured puts lets investors collect premium while waiting for a limit order fill on a stock they already want to own.

00:01:28.780 --> 00:01:39.240
Today's market volatility makes the approach relevant because wide bid-ask spreads and headline-driven dips create premium income on names that would otherwise leave cash idle.

00:01:39.960 --> 00:01:50.060
Implementation requires choosing liquid underlines, setting the strike at or below your target entry price, and ensuring the premium exceeds the expected slippage from waiting.

00:01:50.060 --> 00:02:01.180
The tactic has historically performed best in range bound or mildly bullish regimes where implied volatility stays elevated, but the underlying does not gap lower through the strike.

00:02:01.840 --> 00:02:17.400
Risk is still full downside ownership if assigned, so position size must stay inside normal allocation rules. The method works only on stocks and investor would be happy to own outright, turning idle cash into income while the limit order sits unfilled.

00:02:17.400 --> 00:02:28.140
You can test this directly on a name already held in a TFSA by pulling the options chain and comparing premium at the chosen strike to the cost of simply holding cash.

00:02:28.840 --> 00:02:38.080
Central bank decisions continue to shape rate-sensitive sectors, and today's neutral rate estimate keeps that path in focus without forcing immediate repricing.

00:02:38.080 --> 00:02:46.820
Disclaimer, this is a simulated trade for educational purposes only. No real money is involved. This is not financial advice.

00:02:47.540 --> 00:02:59.880
Today's pick is NFI.TO, NFI Group on the TSX in the industrial sector. The strategy is a catalyst-driven entry on domestic demand recovery narrative for transit equipment.

00:02:59.880 --> 00:03:13.320
The hold period is five sessions from entry, and the rule is fixed. Invalidation occurs if Canadian transit orders in the next quarterly fall below the prior year level, at which point the demand thesis is dead.

00:03:13.960 --> 00:03:20.280
The catalyst comes from Canadian demand recovery theme highlighted amid broader TSX rotation away from metals.

00:03:20.280 --> 00:03:29.520
Technical setup shows the stock trading near recent session highs with no 20-day volume spike yet, and support sits at the 50-day moving average.

00:03:30.200 --> 00:03:40.480
Risk assessment notes that a geopolitical oil spike could raise input costs, with the stop derived from the invalidation level capping model lost near 6-8%.

00:03:40.480 --> 00:03:47.340
Target is plus 3% to plus 6% over the five session window, if domestic orders materialize.

00:03:47.340 --> 00:03:55.760
Confidence level is medium because the domestic demand narrative is plausible, but lacks the volume confirmation required for higher conviction.

00:03:56.120 --> 00:04:08.280
This setup forces explicit linkage between a macro theme and a single observable quarterly metric, showing how to convert sector commentary into a testable entry rather than a vague bullish view.

00:04:08.800 --> 00:04:14.540
It also demonstrates sector rotation discipline by moving outside the concentrated names from recent trades.

00:04:14.540 --> 00:04:22.820
Yesterday's weekly hold was IPCO.TO on a buyback supported entry via the announced normal course issuer bid.

00:04:23.460 --> 00:04:27.700
