00:08:11.040 --> 00:08:14.980
Professionals always write the exact observable trigger that kills the thesis,

00:08:15.500 --> 00:08:21.860
such as if the next quarterly shows no new drill results by the end of Q4 before the capital is committed.

00:08:22.340 --> 00:08:27.560
That written line becomes the stop loss reference and prevents hindsight rewriting after a loss.

00:08:28.260 --> 00:08:32.700
Most retail investors instead say if it drops or if the market turns,

00:08:32.700 --> 00:08:37.860
which offers no testable condition and turns every exit into an emotional decision.

00:08:38.440 --> 00:08:43.660
The concrete fix is to state the invalidation in one sentence using a specific data release,

00:08:44.300 --> 00:08:47.700
guidance number, or technical level before entering any position.

00:08:48.380 --> 00:08:54.280
This approach converts losses into measurable feedback on the original thesis, rather than vague regret.

